error[E0277]: `Plain` is not a provider the container holds under its own type for the app's lifetime, so it can neither host `#[hooks]`, `#[scheduled]`, `#[listeners]`, `#[indicators]` or `#[processor]` nor be bound `as dyn Trait`
  --> tests/integration/diagnostics/events/listeners_on_a_non_provider.rs:15:6
   |
15 | impl Plain {
   |      ^^^^^ the container holds no singleton of this type
   |
help: the trait `ProviderResidency` is not implemented for `Plain`
  --> tests/integration/diagnostics/events/listeners_on_a_non_provider.rs:12:1
   |
12 | struct Plain;
   | ^^^^^^^^^^^^
   = note: a provider-hosted decorator resolves its host with `Container::get::<Self>()`, outside any request, and `as dyn Trait` holds one instance under its own type beside the trait object, so the type must be a singleton provider. Add `#[injectable]` — or, on a provider registered by hand with `ContainerBuilder::provide`, write `impl ProviderResidency` for it with `const SINGLETON: bool = true`
   = help: the following other types implement trait `ProviderResidency`:
             AbilityGuard<F>
             AllowAllMcpGuard
             GraphqlAbilityBridge<A, G>
             HealthService
             McpAbilityBridge<A, G>
             McpDataContext
             SeaOrmHealthIndicator
             WorkerDbContext
           and $N others
